<article class="env-lemma" id="0E3Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E3Q">Lemma <span data-tag="0E3Q">53.24.6</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$ of dimension $1$ with $H^0(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = k$ having genus $g \geq 2$. Assume the singularities of $X$ are at-worst-nodal and that $X$ has no rational tails. Consider a sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  X = X_0 \to X_1 \to \ldots \to X_ n = X'  \]
</div>
  <p> of contractions of rational bridges (Example <a href="/tag/0E3M" data-tag="0E3M">53.24.1</a>) until none are left. Then $\omega _{X'}$ ample. The morphism $X \to X'$ is independent of choices and formation of this morphism commutes with base field extensions. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We proceed by contracting rational bridges until there are none left. Then $\omega _{X'}$ is ample by Lemma <a href="/tag/0E3P" data-tag="0E3P">53.24.5</a>. 
    <p>
      Denote $f : X \to X'$ the composition. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0E3N" data-tag="0E3N">53.24.4</a> and induction we see that $f^*\omega _{X'} = \omega _ X$. We have $f_*\mathcal{O}_ X = \mathcal{O}_{X'}$ because this is true for contraction of a rational bridge. Thus the projection formula says that $f_*f^*\mathcal{L} = \mathcal{L}$ for all invertible $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-modules $\mathcal{L}$. Hence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \Gamma (X', \omega _{X'}^{\otimes m}) = \Gamma (X, \omega _ X^{\otimes m})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       for all $m$. Since $X'$ is the Proj of the direct sum of these by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C6J" data-tag="0C6J">29.44.17</a> we conclude that the morphism $X \to X'$ is completely canonical. 
    <p>
      Let $K/k$ be an extension of fields, then $\omega _{X_ K}$ is the pullback of $\omega _ X$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0E32" data-tag="0E32">53.4.4</a>) and we have $\Gamma (X, \omega _ X^{\otimes m}) \otimes _ k K$ is equal to $\Gamma (X_ K, \omega _{X_ K}^{\otimes m})$ by Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KH" data-tag="02KH">30.5.2</a>. Thus formation of $f : X \to X'$ commutes with base change by $K/k$ by the arguments given above. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>